<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caffaro di Rustico da Caschifellone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1080–1166</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caffaro di Rustico da Caschifellone (c. 1080–1166) was a Genoese nobleman, consul, diplomat and naval commander who wrote the first official chronicle of the commune of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. He took part in the First Crusade, and his Annals, adopted by the commune in 1152, were continued by official successors until 1294, making them a major source for the history of Genoa and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caffaro-di-rustico-da-caschifellone.jpg" alt="Caffaro di Rustico da Caschifellone" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daderot · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caffaro_di_Rustico_da_Caschifellone_-_Villetta_Di_Negro_(Genoa)_-_DSC02421.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
